WEBVTT

00:02:55.338 --> 00:02:56.517
It's not a dream.

00:02:56.635 --> 00:02:58.614
You ever heard of an
out-Of-Body experience?

00:02:58.649 --> 00:03:00.110
We're spirits...

00:03:01.135 --> 00:03:02.520
Of people close to death.

00:03:04.554 --> 00:03:07.495
Your son is dying, and
you're worried about the colt?

00:03:08.883 --> 00:03:10.981
You shoot me in the heart, son!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.361
You're bringing the
demon here, aren't you?

00:03:14.362 --> 00:03:16.820
Having some stupid, macho showdown!

00:03:17.431 --> 00:03:19.635
If you killed that damn
thing when you had the chance,

00:03:19.646 --> 00:03:21.769
None of this would have happened.

00:03:28.603 --> 00:03:30.157
I want to make a deal.

00:03:31.762 --> 00:03:33.886
You're much prettier than
the last reaper I met.

00:03:33.892 --> 00:03:37.348
I will give you the colt and the
bullet. But you got to help Dean.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:40.417
So, we have a deal?

00:03:40.992 --> 00:03:43.216
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:03:45.581 --> 00:03:47.536
Today is your lucky day, kid.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:51.877
You watch out for Sammy, okay?

00:04:00.271 --> 00:04:01.305
Okay.

00:04:01.692 --> 00:04:02.597
Dad?

00:04:06.491 --> 00:04:08.456
Time of death, 10:41 a.M.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:37.527
God, I hate clowns. Always creep me out.

00:04:37.532 --> 00:04:39.087
Shh! She likes them.

00:04:48.611 --> 00:04:49.896
Last ride, Nora.

00:05:03.813 --> 00:05:05.485
Look, mom, another clown.

00:05:11.142 --> 00:05:13.096
What are you trying to
do, scare your father?

00:05:13.102 --> 00:05:14.097
Honey.

00:05:30.381 --> 00:05:32.137
Look, mom, a clown.

00:05:36.931 --> 00:05:38.496
You missed him.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.656
Before he...

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:35.855
Before he...

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:42.345
Did he say anything to you?

00:07:44.913 --> 00:07:46.376
About anything?

00:07:53.942 --> 00:07:55.537
No.

00:07:59.521 --> 00:08:00.847
Nothing.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.556
How's the car coming along?

00:08:41.563 --> 00:08:42.487
Slow.

00:08:43.522 --> 00:08:44.437
Yeah?

00:08:45.742 --> 00:08:47.525
You need any help?

00:08:47.533 --> 00:08:49.077
What? You under a hood?

00:08:49.641 --> 00:08:50.817
I'll pass.

00:08:53.393 --> 00:08:54.588
Need anything else, then?

00:08:57.093 --> 00:08:58.177
Stop it, Sam.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:08:59.826
Stop what?

00:08:59.833 --> 00:09:01.157
Stop asking if I need anything.

00:09:01.172 --> 00:09:03.625
Stop asking if I'm okay. I'm okay.

00:09:03.992 --> 00:09:05.937
Really. I promise.

00:09:09.761 --> 00:09:11.458
All right, Dean, it's just...

00:09:12.761 --> 00:09:15.985
We've been at Bobby's for over a week
now, and you haven't brought up dad once.

00:09:17.651 --> 00:09:19.075
You know what? You're right.

00:09:20.172 --> 00:09:21.106
Come here.

00:09:21.541 --> 00:09:23.415
I'm gonna lay my head
gently on your shoulder.

00:09:23.571 --> 00:09:25.817
Maybe we could cry, hug,

00:09:25.823 --> 00:09:28.326
Maybe even slow dance.
Don't patronize me, Dean.

00:09:28.331 --> 00:09:31.755
Dad is dead, the colt is gone,
and it seems pretty damn likely

00:09:31.761 --> 00:09:34.397
That the demon is behind all of this.
And you're acting like nothing happened.

00:09:34.402 --> 00:09:35.846
What do you want me to say?
Say something, all right?!

00:09:35.851 --> 00:09:39.127
Hell, say anything! Aren't you
angry? Don't you want revenge?

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:42.735
But all you do is sit out here all day
long buried underneath this damn car.

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:44.735
Revenge, huh? Sounds good. Yeah!

00:09:45.343 --> 00:09:47.228
Got any leads on where the demon is?

00:09:47.230 --> 00:09:50.005
Making heads or tails of any of
dad's research? 'Cause I sure ain't.

00:09:50.009 --> 00:09:51.667
You know, when we do finally find it...

00:09:51.672 --> 00:09:52.735
Oh,

00:09:52.743 --> 00:09:54.688
No, wait, like you
said, the colt's gone.

00:09:54.691 --> 00:09:56.567
But I'm sure you figured
out another way to kill it.

00:09:56.742 --> 00:09:59.055
We've got nothing, Sam. Nothing, okay?

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:01.907
The only thing I can do
is I can work on the car.

00:10:04.081 --> 00:10:05.745
Well, we got something, all right?

00:10:06.632 --> 00:10:08.256
It's what I came out here to tell you.

00:10:08.262 --> 00:10:09.726
It's one of dad's old phones.

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:13.006
It took me a while, but I cracked
his voice mail code. Listen to this.

00:10:17.082 --> 00:10:19.168
<i>John, it's Ellen... Again.</i>

00:10:19.451 --> 00:10:22.235
<i>Look, don't be stubborn. You
know I can help you. Call me.</i>

00:10:23.671 --> 00:10:25.315
That message is four months old.

00:10:25.322 --> 00:10:27.105
Dad saved that chick's
message for four months?

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:28.346
Yeah. Who's Ellen?

00:10:28.353 --> 00:10:30.017
Any mention of her in dad's journal? No,

00:10:30.021 --> 00:10:32.565
But I ran a trace on the
number, and I got an address.

00:10:35.343 --> 00:10:37.137
Ask Bobby if we can use one of his cars.

00:10:48.702 --> 00:10:50.416
This is humiliating.

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:56.446
I feel like a friggin' soccer mom.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:58.735
It's the only car Bobby had running.

00:11:01.713 --> 00:11:03.065
H ello?

00:11:05.081 --> 00:11:06.836
Anybody here? Alright.

00:11:06.842 --> 00:11:09.057
Hey, did you bring the... Of course.

00:11:38.331 --> 00:11:39.657
Hey, buddy?

00:11:43.592 --> 00:11:46.087
I'm guessing that isn't Ellen. Yeah.

00:12:04.083 --> 00:12:06.207
Oh, god, please let that be a rifle.

00:12:06.962 --> 00:12:08.786
No, I'm just real happy to see you.

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:11.654
Don't move. Not moving. Copy that.

00:12:13.173 --> 00:12:14.645
You should know something, miss.

00:12:14.721 --> 00:12:16.405
When you put a rifle on someone,

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:18.506
You don't want to put it
right against their back,

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.888
'Cause it makes it real easy to do...

00:12:23.631 --> 00:12:24.657
That!

00:12:25.721 --> 00:12:26.678
Sam!

00:12:27.071 --> 00:12:28.424
I need some help in here.

00:12:28.432 --> 00:12:30.048
I can't see. I can't even see!

00:12:30.202 --> 00:12:31.275
Sorry, Dean.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.868
I can't right now. I'm a...

00:12:34.392 --> 00:12:35.758
Little  tied up.

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:39.787
Sam? Dean?

00:12:41.789 --> 00:12:42.878
Winchester?

00:12:44.112 --> 00:12:44.946
Yeah.

00:12:45.853 --> 00:12:47.007
Son of a bitch.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:48.297
Mom, you know these guys?

00:12:48.303 --> 00:12:50.625
Yeah,  I think these are
John Winchester's boys.

00:12:54.039 --> 00:12:55.006
Hey, I'm Ellen.

00:12:55.452 --> 00:12:56.708
That's my daughter, Jo.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:58.745
Hey.

00:12:59.291 --> 00:13:00.718
You're not gonna hit me again, are you?

00:13:01.893 --> 00:13:02.955
Here you go.

00:13:02.962 --> 00:13:03.907
Thanks.

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:09.057
You called our dad, said you could help.

00:13:09.691 --> 00:13:10.807
Help with what?

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.615
Well,

00:13:13.773 --> 00:13:15.177
The demon, of course.

00:13:17.011 --> 00:13:18.607
I heard he was closing in on it.

00:13:19.692 --> 00:13:22.228
Was there an article in "the demon
hunter's quarterly" that I missed?

00:13:22.231 --> 00:13:23.885
I mean, who are you? How
do you know about all this?

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:25.518
Hey, I just run a saloon.

00:13:26.132 --> 00:13:29.626
But hunters have been known
to pass through now and again,

00:13:29.743 --> 00:13:31.768
Including your dad a long time ago.

00:13:31.782 --> 00:13:33.347
John was like family once. Oh yeah?

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.145
I mean he's never mentioned you before.

00:13:36.152 --> 00:13:38.065
You'd have to ask him that.

00:13:40.912 --> 00:13:42.597
So, why exactly do we need your help?

00:13:42.602 --> 00:13:44.424
Hey, don't do me any favors.

00:13:44.740 --> 00:13:46.375
Look, if you don't want my help, fine.

00:13:46.381 --> 00:13:48.408
Don't let the door smack
your ass on the way out.

00:13:48.566 --> 00:13:50.229
But John wouldn't have sent you if...

00:13:56.283 --> 00:13:57.414
He didn't send you.

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.250
He's all right, isn't he?

00:14:07.061 --> 00:14:07.937
No.

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:10.424
No, he isn't.

00:14:10.812 --> 00:14:12.875
It was the demon, we think.

00:14:13.903 --> 00:14:16.376
It just got him before
he got it, I guess.

00:14:20.212 --> 00:14:22.138
I'm so sorry. It's okay.

00:14:22.363 --> 00:14:23.628
We're all right.

00:14:23.809 --> 00:14:25.758
Really, I know how
close you and your dad...

00:14:25.759 --> 00:14:27.186
Really, lady, I'm fine.

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:33.407
So, look, if you can help...

00:14:34.681 --> 00:14:36.798
We could use all the help we can get.

00:14:37.172 --> 00:14:38.596
Well, we can't.

00:14:39.902 --> 00:14:41.178
But Ash will.

00:14:41.182 --> 00:14:43.116
Who's Ash? Ash!

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.036
What?

00:14:48.009 --> 00:14:49.626
Closing time?

00:14:51.789 --> 00:14:53.027
That's Ash?

00:14:54.011 --> 00:14:55.028
He's a genius.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.015
You got to be kidding
me. This guy's no genius.

00:15:00.019 --> 00:15:01.868
He's a Lynyrd Skynyrd roadie.

00:15:02.383 --> 00:15:04.616
I like you. Thanks.

00:15:04.802 --> 00:15:06.086
Just give him a chance.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:11.995
All right.

00:15:13.423 --> 00:15:16.715
Well, this stuff's about a
year's worth of our dad's work. So

00:15:17.581 --> 00:15:18.977
Let's see what you make of it.

00:15:29.853 --> 00:15:34.846
Come on. This crap ain't real. Ain't
nobody can track a demon like this.

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:40.118
Our dad could.

00:15:43.133 --> 00:15:45.616
These are nonparametric
statistical overviews,

00:15:45.621 --> 00:15:48.657
Cross-Spectrum correlations. I mean...

00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:50.467
Damn!

00:15:51.901 --> 00:15:53.498
They're signs,

00:15:54.019 --> 00:15:57.565
Omens. If you can track them,
you can track this demon.

00:15:57.572 --> 00:16:01.506
You know, like crop
failures, electrical storms.

00:16:01.511 --> 00:16:05.437
You ever been struck by
lightning? It ain't fun.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:09.386
Can you track it or not?
Yeah, with this, I think so.

00:16:09.402 --> 00:16:12.475
But it's gonna take time. Give me...

00:16:14.309 --> 00:16:16.448
51 hours.

00:16:22.402 --> 00:16:23.745
Hey, man! Yeah?

00:16:23.759 --> 00:16:26.207
By the way, I dig the haircut.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:29.475
All business up front,

00:16:29.611 --> 00:16:31.276
Party in the back.

00:16:44.273 --> 00:16:45.725
Hey, Ellen, what is that?

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:48.316
It's a police scanner.

00:16:48.322 --> 00:16:52.968
We keep tabs on things. No,
no, no, no. The... folder.

00:17:00.772 --> 00:17:03.275
I was gonna give this
to a friend of mine, but

00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:04.927
Take a look

00:17:04.932 --> 00:17:05.836
If you want.

00:17:07.631 --> 00:17:08.345
Thanks.

00:17:09.753 --> 00:17:11.718
How did your mom get
into this stuff, anyway?

00:17:11.722 --> 00:17:12.715
My dad.

00:17:12.951 --> 00:17:14.028
He was a hunter.

00:17:15.442 --> 00:17:16.677
He passed away.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.424
I'm sorry.

00:17:19.883 --> 00:17:21.077
It was a long time ago.

00:17:21.573 --> 00:17:22.736
I was just a kid.

00:17:24.753 --> 00:17:26.126
Sorry to hear about yo dad.

00:17:28.153 --> 00:17:28.995
Yeah.

00:17:32.019 --> 00:17:32.756
So,

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:36.307
I guess I got 51 hours to waste.

00:17:36.603 --> 00:17:38.286
Maybe tonight we should...

00:17:44.792 --> 00:17:46.378
Oh, you know what? Never mind.

00:17:47.081 --> 00:17:49.478
What? Nothing, just...

00:17:50.903 --> 00:17:52.228
Wrong place, wrong time.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:54.698
I thought you were gonna toss
me some cheap pickup line.

00:17:54.702 --> 00:17:58.148
Most hunters come through that door,
think they can get in my pants with some

00:17:58.662 --> 00:18:01.766
Pizza, a six-Pack and
side one of "Zeppelin 4".

00:18:03.093 --> 00:18:04.886
What a bunch of scumbags.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:07.658
Not you.

00:18:08.901 --> 00:18:10.176
I guess not.

00:18:12.163 --> 00:18:13.708
Dean, come here. Check this out.

00:18:15.333 --> 00:18:16.315
Yeah.

00:18:17.383 --> 00:18:21.178
A few murders not far from
here that Ellen caught wind of.

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:23.067
Looks to me like there might be a hunt.

00:18:23.071 --> 00:18:25.398
Yeah, so? So,

00:18:25.402 --> 00:18:26.904
I told her we'd check it out.

00:18:28.182 --> 00:18:30.525
You got to be kidding me. Killer clown?

00:18:30.529 --> 00:18:33.775
Yeah, he left the daughter
unharmed and killed the parents.

00:18:33.779 --> 00:18:35.245
Ripped them to pieces, actually.

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.285
And this family was at
some carnival that night?

00:18:37.293 --> 00:18:39.917
Right, the Cooper carnival.

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:42.715
How do you know we're not dealing
with some psycho carny in a clown suit?

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:47.115
The cops have no leads, and all the
employees were tearing down shop...

00:18:47.122 --> 00:18:51.125
Alibis all around. Plus the girl said
she saw a clown vanish into thin air.

00:18:51.131 --> 00:18:54.567
Cops are saying trauma, of course.
I know what you're thinking, Sam.

00:18:54.573 --> 00:18:56.684
"Why did it have to be clowns?"

00:18:57.161 --> 00:18:58.538
Oh, give me a break.

00:18:58.541 --> 00:19:00.235
You didn't think I remembered, did you?

00:19:01.092 --> 00:19:04.957
Come on, you still bust out crying whenever
you see Ronald Mcdonald on the television.

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:06.305
At least I'm not afraid of flying.

00:19:06.311 --> 00:19:08.795
Planes crash! And
apparently clowns kill.

00:19:12.612 --> 00:19:14.728
So, these types of murders,
they ever happen before?

00:19:15.282 --> 00:19:18.465
Uh, according to the file, 1981, the

00:19:18.471 --> 00:19:21.046
Bunker Brothers Circus.

00:19:21.051 --> 00:19:25.015
Same m.O. It happened three different
times, three different locales.

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:29.468
It's weird though. If it is a spirit, it's usually
bound to a specific locale. A house or a town.

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:32.134
How's this one moving from city
to city? Carnival to carnival?

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:33.418
Cursed object, maybe.

00:19:33.700 --> 00:19:36.155
Spirit attaches itself
to something, and the

00:19:36.162 --> 00:19:40.256
Carnival carries it around.
Great. Paranormal scavenger hunt.

00:19:41.033 --> 00:19:43.048
This case was your idea.

00:19:43.053 --> 00:19:46.596
By the way, why is that? You were
awfully quick to jump on this job.

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:49.914
So? So this is not like you, that's all.

00:19:50.442 --> 00:19:53.384
I thought you were hell-Bent
for leather on the demon hunt.

00:19:54.502 --> 00:19:55.817
I don't know. I just think

00:19:55.830 --> 00:19:58.698
Taking this job, it's what
dad would have wanted us to do.

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:01.498
What dad would have wanted? Yeah.

00:20:02.823 --> 00:20:03.825
So?

00:20:07.881 --> 00:20:08.817
Nothing.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.555
Check it out.

00:20:20.903 --> 00:20:21.965
Evan, look.

00:20:23.101 --> 00:20:26.486
Scary! Yeah, dad, scary.

00:20:26.492 --> 00:20:27.488
What's over here?

00:20:33.892 --> 00:20:36.894
You know, when I was your age, this
would have scared the pants off me.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:01.218
Evan.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:02.346
Hey.

00:21:03.992 --> 00:21:04.906
What is it?

00:21:06.641 --> 00:21:07.875
I...

00:21:08.251 --> 00:21:09.636
I saw a clown.

00:21:11.992 --> 00:21:13.494
Don't be afraid of clowns.

00:21:13.811 --> 00:21:16.147
They're nice. They're your friends.

00:21:16.161 --> 00:21:18.346
Okay? Come on.

00:21:31.531 --> 00:21:32.556
Dad.

00:21:34.442 --> 00:21:35.426
Dad!

00:21:37.372 --> 00:21:38.218
Evan.

00:21:38.540 --> 00:21:39.587
What is it?

00:21:40.073 --> 00:21:41.797
You were right.

00:21:42.259 --> 00:21:43.788
He is my friend.

00:22:10.141 --> 00:22:11.155
Check it out.

00:22:11.163 --> 00:22:12.144
Five-O.

00:22:36.722 --> 00:22:37.645
Did you get her number?

00:22:42.190 --> 00:22:44.545
More murders? Two more last night.

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:46.077
Apparently, they were ripped to shreds,

00:22:46.080 --> 00:22:47.875
And they had a little boy with them.

00:22:47.891 --> 00:22:49.605
Who fingered a clown.

00:22:53.631 --> 00:22:54.455
W hat?

00:22:55.103 --> 00:22:57.686
Yes, a clown, who apparently
vanished into thin air.

00:22:58.143 --> 00:23:00.694
Dean, you know, looking for
a cursed object, it's like

00:23:01.220 --> 00:23:04.234
Trying to find a needle in a stack
of needles. It could be anything.

00:23:05.099 --> 00:23:08.367
Well, it's bound to give off emf. So
we'll just have to scan everything.

00:23:08.369 --> 00:23:12.755
Oh, good. That's nice and inconspicuous.

00:23:13.002 --> 00:23:15.036
I guess we'll just have to blend in.

00:23:26.881 --> 00:23:27.907
Excuse me.

00:23:28.251 --> 00:23:30.346
We're looking for a Mr. Cooper.
Have you seen him around?

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.545
What is that? Some kind of joke?

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:38.694
Oh, god, I'm sorry. You think
I wouldn't give my eyeteeth

00:23:38.701 --> 00:23:43.315
To see Mr. Cooper or a
sunset or anything at all?

00:23:43.321 --> 00:23:44.586
Want to give me a little help here?

00:23:44.593 --> 00:23:45.545
Not really.

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:47.555
Hey, Barry, is there a problem?

00:23:48.840 --> 00:23:52.494
Yeah, this guy hates
blind people. No, I don't.

00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:55.616
Hey, buddy, what's your problem? Nothing.
It's just a little misunderstanding.

00:23:55.623 --> 00:23:56.627
Little?

00:23:56.641 --> 00:23:58.586
You son of a bitch. No, no, no!

00:23:58.599 --> 00:24:00.958
Could somebody tell
me where Mr. Cooper is?

00:24:01.510 --> 00:24:02.705
Please?

00:24:02.711 --> 00:24:04.875
You boys picked a hell
of a time to join up.

00:24:05.069 --> 00:24:06.385
Take a seat.

00:24:06.942 --> 00:24:09.507
We got all kinds of local trouble.

00:24:11.280 --> 00:24:12.555
What do you mean?

00:24:12.653 --> 00:24:16.798
A couple of folks got themselves murdered.
Cops always seem to start here first.

00:24:16.802 --> 00:24:19.457
So, you two ever work
the circuit before?

00:24:19.460 --> 00:24:22.756
Uh, yes, sir. Last year
through Texas and Arkansas.

00:24:22.759 --> 00:24:24.394
Doing what?

00:24:25.102 --> 00:24:26.228
Ride jockeys?

00:24:26.643 --> 00:24:27.657
Pull shoot?

00:24:28.511 --> 00:24:30.547
A-And-S men?
Yeah, it's a...

00:24:30.799 --> 00:24:32.355
Little bit of everything, I guess.

00:24:35.041 --> 00:24:38.255
You two have never worked a show
in your lives before, have you?

00:24:39.490 --> 00:24:40.367
Nope.

00:24:41.342 --> 00:24:42.615
But we really need the work.

00:24:44.592 --> 00:24:46.698
And Sam here's got a
thing for the bearded lady.

00:24:51.491 --> 00:24:52.526
You see that picture?

00:24:53.710 --> 00:24:54.724
That's my daddy.

00:24:55.240 --> 00:24:56.276
You look just like him.

00:24:56.451 --> 00:24:57.736
He was in the business.

00:24:58.522 --> 00:25:01.416
Ran a freak show 'til they
outlawed them most places.

00:25:01.642 --> 00:25:05.144
Apparently displaying the
deformed isn't dignified.

00:25:05.151 --> 00:25:08.586
So, most of the performers went
from honest work to rotting in

00:25:08.593 --> 00:25:10.537
Hospitals and asylums.

00:25:11.829 --> 00:25:13.056
That's progress,

00:25:13.609 --> 00:25:14.576
I guess.

00:25:17.089 --> 00:25:18.435
You see, this place

00:25:18.510 --> 00:25:20.366
Is a refuge for outcasts.

00:25:20.531 --> 00:25:21.797
Always has been.

00:25:22.083 --> 00:25:24.375
For folks that don't
fit in nowhere else.

00:25:26.272 --> 00:25:27.184
But you two...

00:25:29.343 --> 00:25:31.057
You should go to school,

00:25:31.710 --> 00:25:33.007
Find a couple of girls,

00:25:33.302 --> 00:25:35.276
Have 2.5 kids,

00:25:35.281 --> 00:25:36.827
Live regular.

00:25:41.423 --> 00:25:42.347
Sir...

00:25:44.692 --> 00:25:45.886
We don't want to go to school.

00:25:46.309 --> 00:25:47.984
And we don't want regular.

00:25:48.741 --> 00:25:50.127
We want this.

00:25:54.150 --> 00:25:55.218
What?

00:25:56.561 --> 00:25:59.425
That whole "I don't want
to go back to school" thing,

00:25:59.630 --> 00:26:00.435
You just...

00:26:01.173 --> 00:26:03.407
You were just saying that
to Cooper, or were you,

00:26:03.752 --> 00:26:04.664
You know,

00:26:04.670 --> 00:26:05.586
Saying it?

00:26:07.583 --> 00:26:09.346
I don't know. You don't know?

00:26:10.361 --> 00:26:12.498
I thought that once the demon was dead

00:26:12.502 --> 00:26:15.694
And the fat lady sings that you were
gonna take off, head back to wussy state.

00:26:16.150 --> 00:26:17.477
I'm having second thoughts.

00:26:18.109 --> 00:26:19.884
Really? Yeah, I think...

00:26:21.712 --> 00:26:23.326
Dad would have wanted
me to stick to the job.

00:26:23.333 --> 00:26:25.154
Since when do you give
a damn what dad wanted?

00:26:25.583 --> 00:26:27.775
You spent half your life doing
exactly what he didn't want.

00:26:27.791 --> 00:26:29.537
Since he died, okay?

00:26:31.423 --> 00:26:32.897
You have a problem with that?

00:26:36.281 --> 00:26:37.676
No, I don't have a problem at all.

00:27:40.770 --> 00:27:41.866
Who is this?

00:28:19.641 --> 00:28:21.115
Hello? Hey, man.

00:28:21.910 --> 00:28:23.816
What's the matter? You sound
like you just saw a clown.

00:28:24.520 --> 00:28:25.487
Very funny.

00:28:27.569 --> 00:28:28.904
Skeleton, actually.

00:28:30.051 --> 00:28:32.445
Like a real human
skeleton? In the fun house.

00:28:32.451 --> 00:28:33.955
Listen, I was thinking. What if

00:28:33.961 --> 00:28:37.086
The spirit isn't attached to a cursed object.
What if it's attached to its own remains.

00:28:37.090 --> 00:28:39.444
Did the bones give off
emf? Well, no, but...

00:28:39.451 --> 00:28:41.488
We should check it out
anyway. I'm heading to you.

00:28:43.932 --> 00:28:46.215
What are you doing here, kid?

00:28:47.491 --> 00:28:49.817
Just sweeping. Bull.

00:28:49.819 --> 00:28:52.596
And what were you
talking about? Skeletons?

00:28:52.602 --> 00:28:54.248
What's emf?

00:28:55.340 --> 00:28:57.625
Dude, your blind-Man
hearing is out of control.

00:28:57.632 --> 00:28:59.806
We're a tight-Knit group.
We don't like outsiders.

00:28:59.810 --> 00:29:02.265
We take care of our own problems.

00:29:03.190 --> 00:29:05.385
We got a problem? You
tell me. You're the one

00:29:05.392 --> 00:29:07.767
Talking about human bones.

00:29:10.740 --> 00:29:12.048
Do you believe in ghosts?

00:29:12.641 --> 00:29:13.416
What?

00:29:13.590 --> 00:29:14.695
My brother and me...

00:29:16.741 --> 00:29:18.055
We're writing a book about them.

00:29:21.113 --> 00:29:22.865
What took you so long? Long story.

00:29:22.871 --> 00:29:24.846
Mommy, look at the clown.

00:29:27.342 --> 00:29:28.478
What clown?

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:34.736
Come on, sweetie. Come on.

00:29:48.900 --> 00:29:50.377
Dean, I cannot believe

00:29:50.382 --> 00:29:52.708
You told Papasian about
the homicidal phantom clown.

00:29:52.711 --> 00:29:55.615
I told him an urban legend
about a homicidal phantom clown.

00:29:55.619 --> 00:29:57.028
I never said it was real. Keep it down.

00:29:59.232 --> 00:30:00.404
Oh, and get this.

00:30:00.413 --> 00:30:02.575
I mentioned the Bunker
Brothers Circus in '81

00:30:02.661 --> 00:30:05.555
And their evil-Clown
apocalypse. Guess what.

00:30:05.559 --> 00:30:06.347
What?

00:30:06.970 --> 00:30:08.986
Before Mr. Cooper owned Cooper carnival,

00:30:09.442 --> 00:30:10.826
He worked for the Bunker Brothers.

00:30:10.832 --> 00:30:12.026
He was their lot manager.

00:30:12.032 --> 00:30:13.944
So you think whatever's
the spirit attached to

00:30:13.962 --> 00:30:16.436
Cooper just brought it with
him? Something like that.

00:30:19.152 --> 00:30:21.244
I can't believe we keep
talking about clowns.

00:30:49.309 --> 00:30:51.266
Want to come in and play?

00:31:05.881 --> 00:31:09.266
Want to see mommy and
daddy? They're upstairs.

00:31:11.211 --> 00:31:12.307
Hey!

00:31:21.962 --> 00:31:23.666
Sam, watch out!

00:31:28.089 --> 00:31:29.708
What's going on in here?

00:31:29.712 --> 00:31:31.965
Oh, my god! What do you do to my
daughter! Get away from my kid!

00:31:31.970 --> 00:31:34.936
Mommy, daddy, they shot my clown.

00:31:45.451 --> 00:31:46.997
You really think they saw our plates?

00:31:48.790 --> 00:31:50.297
I don't want to take the chance.

00:31:50.472 --> 00:31:52.497
Besides, I hate this
freaking thing anyway.

00:31:54.650 --> 00:31:56.307
Well, one thing's for sure.

00:31:56.309 --> 00:31:57.296
What's that?

00:31:58.070 --> 00:31:59.496
We're not dealing with a spirit.

00:31:59.820 --> 00:32:01.595
That rock salt hit something solid.

00:32:01.792 --> 00:32:05.404
Yeah, a person, or maybe a creature
that can make itself invisible?

00:32:05.420 --> 00:32:07.424
Yeah, and dresses up
like a clown for kicks?

00:32:07.430 --> 00:32:08.865
Did it say anything in dad's journal?

00:32:08.882 --> 00:32:09.576
Nope.

00:32:13.163 --> 00:32:13.934
Who you calling?

00:32:14.359 --> 00:32:16.896
Maybe Ellen or that guy
Ash will know something.

00:32:17.660 --> 00:32:19.336
Hey, you think, uh...

00:32:19.932 --> 00:32:21.897
You think dad and
Ellen ever had a thing?

00:32:22.202 --> 00:32:23.127
No way.

00:32:23.420 --> 00:32:25.195
Then why didn't he tell us about her?

00:32:25.580 --> 00:32:27.654
I don't know. Maybe they
had some sort of falling-Out.

00:32:28.583 --> 00:32:29.444
Yeah.

00:32:31.792 --> 00:32:34.425
You ever notice dad had a
falling-Out with just about everybody?

00:32:39.163 --> 00:32:40.787
Don't get all maudlin on me, man.

00:32:40.789 --> 00:32:41.617
What do you mean?

00:32:42.221 --> 00:32:46.035
I mean this strong, silent thing
of yours. It's crap. I'm over it.

00:32:46.039 --> 00:32:48.317
This isn't just anyone we're
talking about. This is dad.

00:32:48.320 --> 00:32:50.038
I know how you felt about the man.

00:32:50.039 --> 00:32:53.226
Back off, all right? Just because I'm
not caring and sharing like you want...

00:32:53.230 --> 00:32:56.167
No, no, no. That's not what this is about,
Dean. I don't care how you deal with this,

00:32:56.170 --> 00:32:57.954
But you have to deal with it, man.

00:32:59.461 --> 00:33:01.765
Listen, I'm your brother, all right?
I just want to make sure you're okay.

00:33:01.772 --> 00:33:03.656
Dude, I'm okay! I'm okay!

00:33:03.662 --> 00:33:05.767
I swear, the next person
who asks me if I'm okay,

00:33:05.770 --> 00:33:07.275
I'm gonna start throwing punches.

00:33:07.470 --> 00:33:09.788
These are your issues.
Quit dumping them on me.

00:33:09.789 --> 00:33:10.734
What are you talking about?

00:33:10.750 --> 00:33:13.576
I just think it's really interesting
this sudden obedience you have to dad.

00:33:13.580 --> 00:33:15.438
It's like, "oh, what
would dad want me to do?"

00:33:15.819 --> 00:33:18.246
You spent your entire life
slugging it out with that man.

00:33:18.251 --> 00:33:20.875
I mean, hell, you picked a fight with
him the last time you ever saw him,

00:33:20.881 --> 00:33:22.915
And now that he's dead,
now you wanna make it right?

00:33:22.920 --> 00:33:25.477
Well, I'm sorry, Sam, but you
can't. It's too little too late.

00:33:25.480 --> 00:33:26.627
Why are you saying this to me?

00:33:26.632 --> 00:33:30.385
I want you to be honest with yourself
about this! I'm dealing with dad's death.

00:33:30.859 --> 00:33:31.757
Are you?

00:33:37.623 --> 00:33:38.685
I'm gonna call Ellen.

00:33:50.461 --> 00:33:51.557
Thanks a lot.

00:33:53.740 --> 00:33:55.026
Rakshasa.

00:33:55.632 --> 00:33:57.977
What's that? Ellen's best guess.

00:33:58.321 --> 00:34:01.996
It's a race of ancient hindu
creatures. They appear in human form,

00:34:02.002 --> 00:34:03.958
They feed on human flesh,

00:34:04.271 --> 00:34:05.967
They can make themselves invisible,

00:34:05.971 --> 00:34:08.746
And they cannot enter a home
without first being invited to.

00:34:08.751 --> 00:34:11.296
They dress up like clowns,
and children invite them in.

00:34:11.300 --> 00:34:13.557
Why don't they just munch
on the kids? No idea.

00:34:13.742 --> 00:34:15.207
Not enough meat on the bones, maybe?

00:34:15.211 --> 00:34:18.548
What else you find out? Apparently,
rakshasas live in squalor.

00:34:18.920 --> 00:34:21.615
They sleep on a bed of dead insects.

00:34:22.512 --> 00:34:25.307
And they have to feed a few
times. Every 20 to 30 years.

00:34:25.311 --> 00:34:27.724
Slow metabolism, I
guess. That makes sense.

00:34:27.731 --> 00:34:30.724
The carnival today, the
Bunker Brothers in '81.

00:34:30.733 --> 00:34:32.986
Probably more before that.

00:34:33.190 --> 00:34:35.325
Sam, who do we know
that worked both shows?

00:34:35.329 --> 00:34:36.996
Cooper? Cooper.

00:34:38.333 --> 00:34:40.195
You know, that picture of his father,

00:34:40.463 --> 00:34:41.684
That looked just like him.

00:34:42.623 --> 00:34:43.957
You think maybe it was him?

00:34:44.842 --> 00:34:46.597
Well, who knows how old he is?

00:34:46.602 --> 00:34:47.916
Ellen say how to kill him?

00:34:48.400 --> 00:34:51.414
Legend goes a dagger made of pure brass.

00:34:53.461 --> 00:34:55.367
I think I know where
to get one of those.

00:34:55.372 --> 00:34:58.576
Well, before we go stabbing things into Cooper,
we're gonna want to make damn sure it's him.

00:34:58.582 --> 00:35:01.258
Oh, you're such a stickler
for details, Sammy.

00:35:01.951 --> 00:35:03.747
All right, I'll round up the blade.

00:35:03.992 --> 00:35:06.125
You go check if Cooper's got bedbugs.

00:35:27.702 --> 00:35:30.247
Well, I got all kinds of knives.

00:35:30.539 --> 00:35:33.085
I don't know if I got
a brass one, though.

00:35:41.760 --> 00:35:42.875
What do you think you're doing?

00:35:45.193 --> 00:35:46.476
Check the trunk.

00:36:03.361 --> 00:36:04.228
You?

00:36:08.481 --> 00:36:09.586
Me.

00:36:23.140 --> 00:36:24.246
All right!

00:36:25.530 --> 00:36:26.735
Jeez.

00:36:28.952 --> 00:36:29.954
Hey!

00:36:30.631 --> 00:36:31.416
Hey!

00:36:32.300 --> 00:36:34.987
So, Cooper thinks I'm a
peeping tom, but it's not him.

00:36:34.990 --> 00:36:36.236
Yeah, so I gathered.

00:36:36.253 --> 00:36:37.977
It's the blind guy. He's here somewhere.

00:36:37.981 --> 00:36:40.157
Well, did you get...
The brass blades? No.

00:36:40.163 --> 00:36:41.715
It's just been one of those days.

00:36:42.981 --> 00:36:44.635
I got an idea. Come on.

00:36:56.253 --> 00:36:58.018
Dean, find the maze, okay?

00:37:37.929 --> 00:37:38.864
Where is it? I don't know.

00:37:38.871 --> 00:37:40.606
Shouldn't we see his
clothes walking around?

00:37:55.481 --> 00:37:57.478
Dean, where is it? I don't know!

00:38:11.782 --> 00:38:14.045
Sam, behind you!

00:38:41.001 --> 00:38:42.606
I hate fun houses.

00:38:57.943 --> 00:38:59.407
You boys did a hell of a job.

00:38:59.572 --> 00:39:01.434
Your dad would be proud. Thanks.

00:39:10.213 --> 00:39:12.387
Oh, yeah, I've got to, uh...

00:39:14.182 --> 00:39:15.476
I've got to go...

00:39:15.911 --> 00:39:17.148
Over there...

00:39:17.429 --> 00:39:18.686
Right now.

00:39:23.581 --> 00:39:25.425
So. So.

00:39:27.030 --> 00:39:28.306
Am I gonna see you again?

00:39:31.199 --> 00:39:32.318
Do you want to?

00:39:34.369 --> 00:39:35.625
I wouldn't hate it.

00:39:36.431 --> 00:39:37.666
Can I be honest with you?

00:39:37.961 --> 00:39:39.077
See, normally,

00:39:39.081 --> 00:39:41.608
I'd be hitting on you so
fast it'd make your head spin.

00:39:41.972 --> 00:39:42.998
But

00:39:44.460 --> 00:39:45.655
These days...

00:39:46.820 --> 00:39:47.648
I don't know.

00:39:48.213 --> 00:39:49.288
Wrong place,

00:39:50.019 --> 00:39:51.375
Wrong time?

00:39:52.961 --> 00:39:54.235
It's okay. I get it.

00:39:57.572 --> 00:39:59.565
Where you guys been?

00:39:59.711 --> 00:40:02.675
I've been waiting for you.
We were working a job, Ash.

00:40:03.992 --> 00:40:06.277
Clowns? Clowns? What the...

00:40:06.282 --> 00:40:07.467
You got something for us, Ash?

00:40:08.382 --> 00:40:09.786
Did you find the demon?

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:11.195
It's nowhere around,

00:40:11.400 --> 00:40:13.114
At least nowhere I can find.

00:40:13.130 --> 00:40:15.885
But if this fugly
bastard raises its head,

00:40:16.382 --> 00:40:20.148
I'll know. I mean, I'm on
it like divine on dog dookie.

00:40:20.150 --> 00:40:21.086
What do you mean?

00:40:21.873 --> 00:40:23.115
I mean

00:40:23.842 --> 00:40:26.996
Any of those signs or omens
appear anywhere in the world,

00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:29.856
My rig will go off like a fire alarm.

00:40:30.730 --> 00:40:31.836
You mind?

00:40:36.269 --> 00:40:37.297
What's up, man?

00:40:39.262 --> 00:40:41.126
Ash, where did you learn to do all this?

00:40:41.132 --> 00:40:45.257
M.I.T., before I got
bounced for fighting.

00:40:47.521 --> 00:40:48.498
M.I.T.?

00:40:48.769 --> 00:40:50.144
It's a school in Boston.

00:40:51.050 --> 00:40:51.856
Okay.

00:40:52.460 --> 00:40:54.007
Give us a call as soon
as you know something?

00:40:54.590 --> 00:40:56.277
S, s, compadre.

00:41:07.431 --> 00:41:08.786
Hey, listen.

00:41:09.621 --> 00:41:12.574
If you boys need a place to stay,
I got a couple beds out back.

00:41:14.092 --> 00:41:15.215
Thanks, but no.

00:41:16.422 --> 00:41:18.025
There's something I got to finish.

00:41:18.032 --> 00:41:18.858
Okay.

00:41:34.172 --> 00:41:35.047
You were right.

00:41:36.583 --> 00:41:37.467
About what?

00:41:42.130 --> 00:41:43.186
About me and dad.

00:41:44.172 --> 00:41:47.077
I'm sorry that the last time I was
with him, I tried to pick a fight.

00:41:47.512 --> 00:41:49.885
I'm sorry that I spent most
of my life angry at him.

00:41:50.032 --> 00:41:51.737
I mean, for all I know, he died

00:41:51.862 --> 00:41:53.195
Thinking that I hate him.

00:41:55.391 --> 00:41:56.547
So, you're right.

00:41:58.693 --> 00:42:00.887
What I'm doing right
now... It is too little.

00:42:03.090 --> 00:42:04.088
It's too late.

00:42:09.532 --> 00:42:10.936
I miss him, man.

00:42:13.900 --> 00:42:15.505
And I feel guilty as hell.

00:42:19.389 --> 00:42:20.766
And I'm not all right...

00:42:22.831 --> 00:42:23.885
Not at all...

00:42:32.619 --> 00:42:33.815
But neither are you.

00:42:35.601 --> 00:42:36.668
That much I know.

00:42:41.010 --> 00:42:42.487
I'll let you get back to work.



00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.875
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
